# Build context of gateway-rust/Dockerfile is the repository root: keep it to the Cargo workspace
# (Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, core/, gateway-rust/ and the manifests + sources of the other members, which
# Cargo needs to resolve the workspace) and drop everything else.
# Build output and dependencies are rebuilt inside the image, never copied from the host.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
# Repository metadata, CI configuration and ignore files have no place in an image.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
# Anything that can hold a secret stays out of the build context.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
# Documentation, the shared test vectors and the other implementations are not needed to build the gateway.
**/*.md
conformance/
docs/
**/docs/
gateway-workers/
# The Rust Worker's test harness, scripts and deploy configuration belong to the Worker, not the gateway image.
worker/tests/
worker/scripts/
worker/build*/
worker/package.json
worker/package-lock.json
worker/wrangler.toml
# Repository scripts (version checks, origin lock) run in CI, not in the image.
scripts/
